# Car Rental System - Project Report

## Executive Summary

This report outlines the **Car Rental System**, a full-stack web application enabling users to browse available vehicles, make reservations, and manage bookings. Built with Python Flask backend and vanilla JavaScript frontend, it ensures secure, real-time interactions with persistent JSON-based data storage.

Key Features:
- JWT authentication for secure user sessions
- Responsive UI design for all devic
- Real-time car availability tracking
- Admin dashboard with statistics and reporting
- License and ID card verification for bookings

Deployment:
- Live URL: https://car-rental-system-vmxn.onrender.com
- Platform: Render (free tier)
- Backend & Frontend: Single deployment serving both API and static files

Tech Stack:
- Backend: Python 3.11, Flask, bcrypt, PyJWT
- Frontend: HTML5, CSS3, Vanilla JavaScript
- Database: JSON file-based storage (cars.json, users.json, bookings.json, admins.json)

Project Goals:
Streamline car rental operations with user-friendly booking interface, admin oversight, persistent data storage, and secure authentication.

---

 1. Project Structure Architecture

# 1.1 Backend (Python + Flask)

app.py: Entry point that initializes Flask application on port 5000 (or environment PORT), handles CORS, defines API routes, and serves frontend files.

```
Backend/
├── app.py              # Main Flask application
├── requirements.txt    # Python dependencies
└── data/              # JSON storage directory
    ├── cars.json      # Car inventory
    ├── users.json     # User accounts
    ├── bookings.json  # Rental bookings
    └── admins.json    # Admin accounts
```

### 1.2 Data Models

The system uses JSON-based storage with the following data structures:

#### 1. User Model
- **Fields:** _id, name, email, password (hashed), phone, created_at
- **Purpose:** Store user account information
- **Security:** Passwords encrypted with bcrypt

#### 2. Car Model
- Fields: _id, name, model, category, price_per_day, seats, transmission, fuel_type, image, features, available, description
- Purpose: Represent available rental vehicles
- Categories: Sedan, SUV, Sports, Electric

#### 3. Booking Model
- Fields: _id, user_id, user_name, user_email, car_id, car_name, car_model, start_date, end_date, days, total_price, license_card, id_card, status, created_at
- Purpose: Track rental reservations
- Statuses:*confirmed, completed, cancelled

#### 4. Admin Model
- Fields: _id, username, password (hashed), created_at
- Purpose: Admin account management
-*Default Admin: username: admin, password: admin123

### 1.3 API Routes

Authentication Routes (/api):
- `POST /api/register` - Create new user accounts
- `POST /api/login` - Authenticate users and generate JWT tokens
- `POST /api/admin/login` - Admin authentication with separate JWT

Car Routes (/api/cars):
- `GET /api/cars` - Retrieve all available cars
- `GET /api/cars/<car_id>` - Get specific car details

Booking Routes (/api/bookings):
- `POST /api/bookings` - Create new car rental booking (requires authentication)
- `GET /api/bookings/user` - Get current user's booking history (requires authentication)

*Admin Routes (/api/admin):
- `GET /api/admin/bookings` - View all system bookings (requires admin auth)
- `GET /api/admin/statistics` - Dashboard statistics including total users, cars, bookings, revenue (requires admin auth)

Frontend Routes:
- `GET /` - Serve homepage (index.html)
- `GET /<path>` - Serve static frontend files (HTML, CSS, JS, images)

### 1.4 Frontend (HTML + CSS + JavaScript)

```
Frontend/
├── css/
│   └── style.css              # Responsive styling
├── js/
│   ├── main.js                # Homepage functionality
│   ├── auth.js                # User registration/login
│   ├── cars.js                # Car browsing with filters
│   ├── booking.js             # Booking form and validation
│   ├── admin-auth.js          # Admin authentication
│   └── admin-dashboard.js     # Admin statistics dashboard
├── index.html                 # Homepage with featured cars
├── register.html              # User registration
├── login.html                 # User login
├── cars.html                  # Browse all cars
├── booking.html               # Car booking form
├── admin-login.html           # Admin login
└── admin-dashboard.html       # Admin dashboard
```

### 1.5 Deployment Configuration

Files:
- `render.yaml` - Render deployment configuration
- `Procfile` - Process definition for Railway/Heroku
- `runtime.txt` - Python version specification (3.11.0)
- `.gitignore` - Exclude data files and cache from version control

